From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mainui: the renderer loaded when none is configured

Video modes showed the first renderer of the list while r_refdll was
empty, also when the launcher had loaded another one with -ref (bare_app
starts the software renderer on the ODROID-GO Advance until one is chosen
in this menu): the menu claimed "GLES3" with the software renderer
running, and Apply would have switched to it. It now shows the renderer
loaded (r_refdll_loaded) until one is configured.

--- a/3rdparty/mainui/menus/VideoModes.cpp
+++ b/3rdparty/mainui/menus/VideoModes.cpp
@@ -174,6 +174,11 @@
 	// get current _configured_ renderer
 	const char *refdll = EngFuncs::GetCvarString( "r_refdll" );
 
+	// none configured yet: the one loaded (-ref of the launcher), not the
+	// first of the list, which would claim a renderer that is not running
+	if( !refdll[0] )
+		refdll = EngFuncs::GetCvarString( "r_refdll_loaded" );
+
 	if( !refdll[0] )
 	{
 		renderers.SetCurrentValue( 0.0f );
